Here's how to implement this in .NET MAUI Shell:

## 1. Override `OnBackButtonPressed` on your page

```csharp
public partial class EditProductPage : ContentPage
{
    private bool _hasUnsavedChanges;

    protected override bool OnBackButtonPressed()
    {
        if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            // Fire-and-forget the async confirmation
            Dispatcher.Dispatch(async () =>
            {
                bool leave = await DisplayAlert(
                    "Unsaved Changes",
                    "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
                    "Discard", "Stay");

                if (leave)
                    await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
            });

            return true; // Cancel the default back navigation
        }

        return false; // Allow normal back navigation
    }
}
```

Returning `true` suppresses the hardware/software back button. The dialog then conditionally navigates.

## 2. Custom "Cancel" toolbar button

In your XAML, replace the default back arrow with a shell back button override and add a toolbar item:

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="MyApp.EditProductPage"
             Shell.BackButtonBehavior="{StaticResource CancelBackButton}">

    <ContentPage.Resources>
        <BackButtonBehavior x:Key="CancelBackButton"
                            TextOverride="Cancel"
                            Command="{Binding CancelCommand}" />
    </ContentPage.Resources>

    <Shell.BackButtonBehavior>
        <BackButtonBehavior TextOverride="Cancel"
                           Command="{Binding CancelCommand}" />
    </Shell.BackButtonBehavior>

    <!-- page content -->
</ContentPage>
```

## 3. ViewModel command with confirmation

```csharp
public ICommand CancelCommand { get; }

public EditProductViewModel()
{
    CancelCommand = new Command(async () =>
    {
        if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            bool leave = await Shell.Current.DisplayAlert(
                "Unsaved Changes",
                "Discard changes?",
                "Discard", "Stay");

            if (!leave) return;
        }

        await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
    });
}
```

## Key points

| Concern | Mechanism |
|---------|-----------|
| Hardware/swipe back | `OnBackButtonPressed()` returning `true` |
| Custom button text | `BackButtonBehavior.TextOverride` |
| Programmatic nav guard | Async confirmation before `GoToAsync("..")` |

> **Note:** `OnBackButtonPressed` doesn't fire for the iOS swipe-back gesture. To cover that, disable it via `Shell.BackButtonBehavior` with `IsEnabled="True"` (which replaces the native back and disables the swipe), or handle `Disappearing` as a fallback on iOS.
